# The ONE reasoning key (ADR 0012): every model — Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, DeepSeek, GLM,
# Kimi, or any custom slug — runs through the OpenRouter gateway on this key. This key pays
# only for the CURATED model list (lib/run-config.ts); custom slugs require the caller to
# supply their own key in the settings panel.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=''
EXA_API_KEY=''
GOOGLE_FACT_CHECK_API_KEY=''
# Optional, OFF by default: enables the embedding re-rank stage (ADR 0010) only when a run sets
# `rerank` AND this key resolves. Leave blank to keep the no-embeddings de-novo path (ADR 0005).
COHERE_API_KEY=''

# Optional: point at a different OpenAI-compatible gateway (Vercel AI Gateway, self-hosted
# LiteLLM, ...) instead of OpenRouter. The key above is sent to whatever is set here.
#   OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=''         # default https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#
# Reliability knobs. A run fans out ~50–60 parallel LLM calls, which can trip the gateway's
# requests-per-minute cap. These bound the load:
#   LLM_MAX_CONCURRENCY=''         # max simultaneous LLM calls per instance (default 5)
#   RATE_LIMIT_BURST=''            # per-IP request burst on /api/check + /api/summary (default 5)
#   RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN=''          # per-IP sustained requests/minute (default 10)
